WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.542 --> 00:00:04.984
Four chatbots, four bills, and not one of them knows your business.

2
00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:07.956
There's a cheaper way to build your AI team.

3
00:00:07.984 --> 00:00:15.897
This is The One-Person Company, lesson two: pick your stack at twenty, one hundred and three hundred dollars a month.

4
00:00:15.926 --> 00:00:22.698
In this lesson: the tool families, three starter stacks, and the rules that stop subscriptions creeping.

5
00:00:22.746 --> 00:00:24.913
Start with one main office.

6
00:00:24.933 --> 00:00:32.492
That's the tool where your files, instructions and connectors live, because that memory doesn't move between vendors.

7
00:00:32.515 --> 00:00:37.458
Then add a specialist only for a job you named, like Cursor for the website.

8
00:00:37.478 --> 00:00:41.821
At twenty dollars, you get one main office and free tools.

9
00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:46.171
At around one hundred, a stronger office plus one specialist.

10
00:00:46.191 --> 00:00:53.246
At around three hundred, two offices and a department of agents, but only when they replace real hours.

11
00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:59.066
Watch usage as well as price, because background agents use your plan's limits.

12
00:00:59.086 --> 00:01:03.824
And check prices and regions on the vendor's own page before you buy.

13
00:01:03.866 --> 00:01:06.294
First, let's meet the tool families.

